# Free models a default `dispatch.sh opencode` task (and every clawock-patrol round) tries, in
# order: one attempt per line, then a second lap (the runner allows 2 attempts per pool line).
# The pool is read at dispatch time, so edits apply without restarting the patrol service.
#
# Rules for this file
# - Free only (kcn 2026-10-11: "记得别付费的就行"). Every entry must be in the Zen catalog
#   (`opencode models opencode`) with zero cost in https://opencode.ai/zen/v1/models.
#   check-free-pool.py runs at every dispatch and refuses a non-free name or a retired model.
# - This host copy is immutable (chattr +i). To change it: chattr -i, back up, write a temp file,
#   run check-free-pool.py on it, rename it over this one, verify catalog and cost, chattr +i.
#   The repository copy (ops/host/agent-dispatch/) carries the same bytes, so the installer and
#   refresh_live.sh see nothing to restore; change both in the same PR.
# - The order is by what a model's finished rounds turned into, not by whether a probe answers.
#   No switching on output quality at run time (kcn 2026-10-11): the runner moves to the next
#   line only when an attempt stalls or errors.
# - There is no "last resort" position. A model that is only kept because it answers when the
#   others are throttled finishes the round with nothing, and a finished round gives up the
#   area's rotation slot (a failed one keeps it for two retries) and counts in the denominator
#   of P0+P1 per finished round. A model is either good enough to go first or it is not here.
#
# Record, 10-01..10-11 (patrol issues by the model that finished the round; "rejected" = closed
# not planned or patrol:noise; "answered" = attempts of 10-09..10-11 that were not a stall/error):
#
#   model                      finished  P0+P1  per round  empty rounds  rejected/closed  answered
#   space-bunny-free              155      31     0.20        10%            8/289          8/61
#   mimo-v2.6-flash-free            9       3     0.33        11%            0/16           1/53
#   longcat-2.5-preview-free       16       2     0.12        50%            0/13           2/63
#   step-5-preview-free             8       0     0.00        12%            0/6            8/29
#   nemotron-3.5-lightning-free    14       1     0.07        86%            0/4           14/16   (removed)
#   ling-3.1-flash-free             2       0     0.00        50%            0/1            1/52   (removed)
#   nemotron-3-ultra-free          22       1     0.05        27%           38/50             -     (removed 10-08)
#
# 2026-10-11 order and why:
# 1. space-bunny-free: the only large sample, and the best one (0.20 P0+P1 per finished round over
#    155 rounds, 8 of 289 closed issues rejected). Same area, same day, same code on 10-11: the
#    round nemotron-3.5 finished filed nothing, the one space-bunny finished filed a P1 and a P2.
#    It is throttled most of the day now (8 of 61 attempts answered); being first costs one
#    stalled attempt when it is, and gets the round when it is not.
# 2. step-5-preview-free: answers most often of the four (8 of 29) and nothing it filed was
#    rejected, but 8 finished rounds with no P0/P1 is a small sample, not a quality record.
#    kcn put it first on 10-10 ("it is the newest model, it should go forward") and on 10-11
#    left the order to be decided on the record; it goes back to first when its P0+P1 per
#    finished round passes space-bunny's over at least 20 rounds.
# 3. mimo-v2.6-flash-free: best rate, 9 rounds, almost never answering (1 of 53).
# 4. longcat-2.5-preview-free: 0.12 over 16 rounds, half of them empty; 2 of 63 answered.
# Removed 2026-10-11:
#   * nemotron-3.5-lightning-free: answered 14 of 16 times, i.e. it finished the rounds nobody
#     else could start (five silent stalls ahead of it, then a fresh session of its own, not a
#     damaged one), and 12 of those 14 rounds filed nothing. Those were money, logic, automation
#     and recent slots. Without it such a round fails and the area keeps its slot.
#   * ling-3.1-flash-free: 1 of 52 attempts answered in three days; 2 finished rounds ever.
# Removed earlier (check-free-pool.py refuses them): exo-free (HTTP 410 ModelDeprecated),
# fledge-alpha-free (out of the catalog), nemotron-3-ultra-free (38 of 50 issues rejected),
# muse-spark-1.3-contributor-free, ling-3.0-flash-fin-free, mimo-v2.5-free, union-alpha.
# Left out on purpose: big-pickle (silent for 45s in a probe, 200k context). opencode-go is not
# an option: no active subscription, and it is paid.
#
# Free-tier behaviour (unchanged, for whoever reads a slow day): the limit is per model (HTTP 429
# FreeUsageLimitError); space-bunny and mimo retry it silently, so a throttled attempt is only
# ended by the runner's first-event stall limit (210s since 10-11). From about 01:00 to 08:00
# nothing useful answers. There is no verified reset time; do not promise one.
#
# Before adding a model or moving one up, check what its issues became (label `patrol`, closed as
# not planned / `patrol:noise`), not only whether it answers:
#   /root/tools/agent-dispatch/probe-free-models.sh --tool <model>
